-- title:
--   Geometric fibres of the descended Mumford-tower quotient map
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ is a prime and the following data are fixed.
--
--   **Coefficient ring.** $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain together with: the hypothesis `hdvr` that it is a discrete valuation ring, an element $\pi$ with `hπ` asserting $\pi$ irreducible, `hcomplete` asserting that $\mathcal O$ is adically complete for $(\pi)$, `hres` asserting that the residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements, and `hunr` asserting the equality of ideals $(r)=(\pi)$. Further, $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero field which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra and a fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Unramified extension and Frobenius lift.** $\mathrm{Onr}$ is a characteristic-zero domain and $\mathcal O$-algebra, $\mathrm{Fr}$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism of it, subject to: `hOnr_complete`, adic completeness for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$; `hOnr_max`, maximality of that ideal; `hOnr_alg`, every $x\in\mathrm{Onr}$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi\,\mathrm{Onr}$; `hOnr_closed`, every monic polynomial over $\mathrm{Onr}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi\,\mathrm{Onr}$; and `hFr`, $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod{\pi\,\mathrm{Onr}}$ for all $x$.
--
--   **Determinant valuation.** $\mathrm{vdet}:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) is a group homomorphism, and `hvdet` asserts that $\mathrm{vdet}(g)=n$ holds precisely when $\det g=u\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Arithmetic group.** $G$ is a group, $\sigma:G\to\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ a homomorphism and $\Gamma\le G$ a subgroup, with `hcent`: some $z\in\Gamma$ has $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix and $\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma z)=2$; `hodd`: some $w\in\Gamma$ has $\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma w)=1$; and $\Gamma'\le G$ characterised by `hΓ'`: $x\in\Gamma'$ iff $x\in\Gamma$ and $\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma x)$ is even. Next, $\rho:G\to\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ with `hρ`: $\rho g$ is the class of $\sigma g$; `hdisc`: for every vertex $v$ of the lattice tree of $(\mathcal O,K_0)$ the set of elements of $\rho(\Gamma')$ fixing $v$ is finite; `hcocpt`: there is a finite set $S$ of vertices such that every vertex is carried into $S$ by some element of $\rho(\Gamma')$.
--
--   **The Mumford tower.** $g_1\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ has matrix $\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$ (`hg₁`). $N\le \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ satisfies `hNle`: $N\le\rho(\Gamma')$; `hNnorm`: $N$ is normal as a subgroup of $\rho(\Gamma)$; `hNidx`: the relative index of $N$ in $\rho(\Gamma')$ is nonzero. Finally $\mathrm{DM}$ is a `MumfordTower 𝒪 π K₀ r g₁ N`: a tower of schemes $Z_n$ with proper flat structure morphisms $\mathrm{zb}_n:Z_n\to\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$, cartesian transition maps $\mathrm{zt}_n$, affine neighbourhoods of finite sets, and a system of period maps $\mathrm{DM}.q\,n\,B\,h_B:(\Omega\,K_0\,\pi).\mathrm{obj}\,B\to \mathrm{Hom}(\operatorname{Spec}B,Z_n)$ defined for $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ in which $\pi^{n+1}=0$, natural in $B$, compatible with the tower, invariant under $N$ in the pullback sense, and with open-immersion charts.
--
--   Here $(\Omega\,K_0\,\pi).\mathrm{obj}\,B$ is the set of Deligne data over $B$: an assignment, to each full $\mathcal O$-lattice $M\subset K_0^2$, of a $B$-submodule $\mathrm{line}\,M\subseteq B\otimes_{\mathcal O}M$ with invertible quotient, monotone in $M$, equivariant for homotheties by scalar matrices, and satisfying the nondegeneracy condition at every prime of $B$ recorded in `DeligneDatum`. For $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, `DeligneDatum.IsPullback B g d d'` means $d'.\mathrm{line}\,M=(d.\mathrm{line}(g\cdot M))$ pulled back along the base-changed action of $g$, for every full lattice $M$.
--
--   **The twisted tower over the quadratic unramified extension.** Write $\mathcal O_2$ for `AlgHom.equalizer` of $\mathrm{Fr}\circ\mathrm{Fr}$ and the identity, i.e. the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{Onr}$ fixed by $\mathrm{Fr}^2$, and $\mathcal O_2^{(n)}:=\mathcal O_2/(\pi^{n+1})$. The data are: schemes $X_n$, morphisms $\mathrm{xb}_n:X_n\to\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$ and $\mathrm{xt}_n:X_n\to X_{n+1}$; a finite group $G_2$ with homomorphisms $a_n:G_2\to\mathrm{Aut}(X_n)$; morphisms $\mathrm{pr}_1^{n}:X_n\to Z_n$ and $\mathrm{pr}_2^{n}:X_n\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_2^{(n)}$; a homomorphism $\theta:\Gamma\to G_2$; and $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphisms $\mathrm{Fr}_2^{n}$ of $\mathcal O_2^{(n)}$. These are constrained by: `hcart`, each square formed by $\mathrm{xt}_n$, $\mathrm{xb}_n$, $\mathrm{xb}_{n+1}$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the quotient factor map $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+2}\to\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$ is a pullback; `hproper` and `hflat`, each $\mathrm{xb}_n$ is proper and flat; `haff`, every finite subset of $X_n$ is contained in an affine open; `ha_over`, each $a_n(g)$ lies over $\mathrm{xb}_n$; `ha_xt`, $a_n(g)$ followed by $\mathrm{xt}_n$ equals $\mathrm{xt}_n$ followed by $a_{n+1}(g)$; `hX`, each square formed by $\mathrm{pr}_1^{n}$, $\mathrm{pr}_2^{n}$, $\mathrm{zb}_n$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the induced map $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}\to\mathcal O_2^{(n)}$ is a pullback; `hxb`, $\mathrm{xb}_n=\mathrm{pr}_1^{n}$ followed by $\mathrm{zb}_n$; `hxt₁` and `hxt₂`, $\mathrm{pr}_1$ and $\mathrm{pr}_2$ are compatible with the transition maps of the two towers; `hθsurj`, $\theta$ is surjective; `hθker`, $\theta\gamma=1$ iff $\rho(\gamma)\in N$; `hFr₂`, $\mathrm{Fr}_2^{n}$ is induced by $\mathrm{Fr}$ on $\mathcal O_2$ modulo $\pi^{n+1}$; `ha_pr₂`, for $\gamma\in\Gamma$ the automorphism $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_2^{n}$ equals $\mathrm{pr}_2^{n}$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $(\mathrm{Fr}_2^{n})^{-\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma\gamma)}$; and `ha_pr₁`, for $\gamma\in\Gamma$, any $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi^{n+1}=0$, any Deligne data $P,P'$ over $B$ with `DeligneDatum.IsPullback` for $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$ relating $P$ to $P'$, and any $x:\operatorname{Spec}B\to X_n$ with $x$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_1^{n}$ equal to $\mathrm{DM}.q\,n\,B\,h_B\,P$, the morphism $x$ followed by $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ and then $\mathrm{pr}_1^{n}$ equals $\mathrm{DM}.q\,n\,B\,h_B\,P'$.
--
--   **The quotient and the map $q$.** $\mathrm{DQ}$ is a `TowerQuotientDatum 𝒪 π X xb xt G₂ a`: schemes $Y_n$ with proper flat structure morphisms $\mathrm{yb}_n$ to $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$ and cartesian transition maps $\mathrm{yt}_n$, together with morphisms $\mathrm{DQ}.p\,n:X_n\to Y_n$ over the base, compatible with the towers and cartesian over $\mathrm{yt}_n$, invariant under the $G_2$-action, finite, surjective, locally epimorphic, and with the local universal property recorded in that structure. Finally $q$ assigns, to each level $n$, each $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi^{n+1}=0$ in $B$ and each pair $(\psi,P)$ consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi:\mathrm{Onr}\to B$ and a Deligne datum $P$ over $B$, a morphism $\operatorname{Spec}B\to Y_n$; the hypothesis `hqdef` requires $q$ to be computed by charts: whenever $\psi_2:\mathcal O_2^{(n)}\to B$ is an $\mathcal O$-algebra map with $\psi_2\circ(\text{reduction})=\psi|_{\mathcal O_2}$ (`hψ₂`), $P$ is a Deligne datum over $B$ and $x:\operatorname{Spec}B\to X_n$ satisfies $x$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_1^{n}$ $=\mathrm{DM}.q\,n\,B\,h_B\,P$ and $x$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_2^{n}$ $=\operatorname{Spec}\psi_2$, then $q\,n\,B\,h_B\,(\psi,P)=x$ followed by $\mathrm{DQ}.p\,n$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every level $n$, every algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi^{n+1}=0$ in $k$, and every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi:\mathrm{Onr}\to k$, both of the following hold.
--
--   (i) *(Surjectivity on geometric points.)* For every morphism $\eta:\operatorname{Spec}k\to Y_n$ such that $\eta$ followed by $\mathrm{yb}_n$ and then by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathcal O\to\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $\mathcal O\to k$, there exists a Deligne datum $P$ over $k$ with $q\,n\,k\,h_k\,(\psi,P)=\eta$.
--
--   (ii) *(Description of fibres.)* For all Deligne data $P,P'$ over $k$, the equality $q\,n\,k\,h_k\,(\psi,P)=q\,n\,k\,h_k\,(\psi,P')$ holds if and only if there is $\gamma\in\Gamma$ with `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct π Onr Fr vdet k (σ γ) (ψ, P) (ψ, P')`, that is: $\psi$ equals `frobTwist Onr Fr` applied to $\psi$ with exponent $-\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma\gamma)$ (the twist of $\psi$ by that power of the Frobenius lift $\mathrm{Fr}$), and for every full lattice $M\subset K_0^2$ the line $P'.\mathrm{line}\,M$ is the pullback of $P.\mathrm{line}\big((\sigma\gamma)^{-1}\cdot M\big)$ along the base change to $k$ of the action of $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$.
--
--   This is the geometric half of the fibre analysis for the descended period map of the twisted Mumford tower in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation: over an algebraically closed residue coefficient field $k$ killed by $\pi^{n+1}$, the map $(\psi,P)\mapsto q_n(\psi,P)$ hits every $k$-point of the quotient $Y_n$ lying over the given $\mathcal O$-structure, and its fibres are exactly the orbits of the twisted $\Gamma$-action on pairs. It is combined with the corresponding statement over $\pi$-adic test rings in [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_fib_adicFib`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_fib_adicFib).
